<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodore I Laskaris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1174–1221</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Theodore Laskaris</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodore I Laskaris was the founder of the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>, ruling from 1205 and as crowned emperor from 1208 until 1221. Son-in-law of the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos">Alexios III Angelos</a>, he gathered Byzantine refugees in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1204. He resisted the Latin Empire and in 1211 defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyuk-menderes-river">Meander</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaykhusraw-i">Kaykhusraw I</a> was killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodore-i-laskaris.jpg" alt="Theodore I Laskaris" width="320" height="488" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Byzantine scribes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:148_-_Theodore_I_Laskaris_(Mutinensis_-_color).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
